form’s min.x. Conversely, dx2 is the difference between the player’s min.x and the platform’s
max.x. Whichever of these differences has the lowest absolute value is the minimum overlap
between the two AABBs. In Figure 10.14, the minimum overlap is dy1. If you then add dy1 to the
